  plans of the dark triad as well as  become the gateway to the spade kingdom  which is fantastic that saves us  a lot of screwing around and general  cringe plan dialogue emitting from  villains but narct also serves as a  mechanism into learning more about the  devils and it even introduces us  properly to our second  series stealing character but more  importantly nacht is also able to fill  the void of leadership left by  army and even the wizard king to be  honest because yeah i get it you're  there but you're  not doing anything the point in keeping  you alive still  remains to be seen knocked on the other  hand is pretty damn functional and quite  seamlessly integrated dodging questions  about where he's been prior to this by  both being on a mission and the fact  that he  hates the black bulls a bit awkward but  yeah i also very much enjoy that his  vice captaincy was decided  more or less arbitrarily it reminds me  of the sort of thing that isaac netro  would do in hunter hunter by making  paris and his vice german solely due to  the fact that he finds paristan annoying  although narc comes into the series  packed with one line as my favorite of  which was if you don't want to be judged  by the way you look then don't look like  that  which yeah obviously doesn't always work  depending on what we're talking about  but it is decent general life advice i  mean for example if you don't want  people to judge you as a slob  then don't look like one put in 20  minutes half an hour every day to make  sure you look decent and then  bam good life successful i like it  knocked also just has a ton of sass and  a very clear belief system which i'm not  sure i've quite gotten my head around  yet but i am very fascinated by him so i  suppose we'll just have to wait for his  inevitable tarbeta micro flashback to  get the full picture but yeah that works  for me they do also like tabata  continuing his trend of naming various  leader figures after light and dark this  time  knocked of course being the german word  for night but narct also brings some  pretty amazing developments with him  deciding to train astor to be the  ultimate weapon which of course brings  us to lead i am so glad that asta's  devil finally has the name but we were  blessed with far more than just that we  also have an entire backstory and some  sense of how devil culture operates  and well it's almost exactly the same as  human culture what a surprise were we  the monsters all along the answer is yes  but lieb is basically devil astor having  been born without magic and becoming  something of an outcast standing up in  the human realm but then still being an  outcast before he met  a certain elicitor a name that i'm not  entirely certain how to pronounce  and this is something that i did not  come anywhere near expecting but this  is astor's mother allegedly although i  should have known better the moment that  juno's heritage was revealed it should  have been a guaranteed deal that we  would see some of asta's heritage as  well because  their journey is a mirrored and that's  just how it is with that said i am still  incredibly curious to know why lisita  abandon asta that's a question we didn't  even come  close to answering in this flashback  actually but i'm sure we'll get around  to it  eventually because lieb does appear to  know a bit more about that matter it was  very touching to see lieb essentially  adopted though and i suppose it actually  makes the banasta brothers in this weird  trans-dimensional mother-sharing  devil-filled kind of way which is also  fantastic because this goes back to the  same idea that we were generally trying  to explore with the elves the concept of  putting race aside and just uniting  around common interests one example of a  common interest being  a generally peaceful existence i suppose  but we now have a supercharged  incarnation of that right now by forging  this bond between  man and devil which will now have to  work together to face these absurdly  escalating threats so yeah let's move on  to that  knocked gives us a lovely explanation of  the plan regarding the seven day advent  an idea that i really like because it  presents us with this nice  game style scenario where we will  inevitably have to deal with seven waves  of devils roaming this world eventually  culminating in one big bad  boss devil and yeah i get that the plan  is to stop this whole thing before that  happens but  well that feels unlikely oh when tarpita  does like the most  tarbeta thing i can think of here by the  way he takes the time to lay out this  complex and very legitimately intriguing  scenario but then when it comes time to  implement it it becomes a ah that was a  bit too  complicated let's let's just do it all  now sort of affair with morris of the  diamond kingdom acting as an accelerator  to  the plan and i really really just need  to emphasize tarpita  always does stuff like this he crafts an  intricate scenario or set of rules and  then almost immediately breaks them the  magic knight ranking system i mentioned  earlier is one example where the system  was put into place but then immediately  rendered meaningless because the ranks  weren't an accurate representation of  anything tangible by the spot of being a  captain same thing with the magic stages  as well we have what like 10 or 11  different stages set up and none of it  matters whatsoever because everyone is  pretty much  already sitting at the top and now here  we have this wonderful seven-day advent  system which also doesn't matter because  we're skipping that and we're just sort  of doing it all right now i mean that's  fine though i'm used to what black  clover is and it does result in exciting  character moments at the very least  and someone we have not yet spoken about  properly here would be yuno i'm loving  his newfound rage field determination  it's a very refreshing take on a  character who is usually capped out in  the realm of  apathetic magic genius and seeing you  know fail is the best thing that has  ever happened to this character because  as a result  i want to see him succeed this time i  legitimately want to i have a desire  whereas previously i've never really  been invested in any other uno fight  prior to this whole zenon affair because  it was always a given that he would just  win because that's you know when winning  is what he does but in this effort you  know is assisted by  language uh language but it does make  sense because they are both gold and  dornies and need to combine their golden  might for the sake of william  etc and so on and so forth but still i  was kind of hoping that the [ __ ]  language arc might have been the last we  saw of him meanwhile noel and select  noel company have been taken in by our  previous antagonist partry and friends  who had vanished without a trace after  the reincarnation arc but it is cool to  see them here because  they will slowly be needed also i  continue to just  love noel in general within this group  she has very much become the natural  leader and very much become another  aster  just slightly smarter but full of just  as much drive and ambition which is  great to see  we've got some big problems to tackle  going forward though one of which is  that power in black clover has long  since gone completely off the charts and  there is no longer really any way of  quantifying how much of a threat  any particular character is except to  keep saying that their power is on a  completely different level to that other  character's power which was already on a  completely different level in and of  itself which has already presented  itself in our first two devil folk both  of whom are very cool and intimidating  as hell by the way i love their designs  but it does get a bit tiring to  consistently blow through that power  ceiling like we already spent  what 30 chapters presenting the dark  triad as completely out of the league of  the cliff kingdom and now we  immediately already have another threat  to deal with that is completely out of  the league of the dark triad but it's  not necessarily these two initial devils  that worry me it's  the the what ain't more to come after  them because the deeper we go the  stronger the devils become so at every  new gate we're going to have to do the  same thing these new devils are on a  completely different level to the  previous devils who were on a completely  different level to the other devils who  were on like a  wow completely different level to the  other devils who were on a completely  different level to the dark triad who  were on a completely different level to  zagret who was on a completely different  level to lick who was on a completely  different level to the clover kingdom in  general  and so on and so forth it's a very  classic shonen trap that many authors  fall into and it's done as an easy way  to escalate the drama of the situation  which  it's working out pretty well here in all  fairness but it is certainly becoming  very hard to see this climax ending in  anything but a sort of ridiculous show  of unearned power from our protagonists  or via some sort of deus ex machina how  do we do both and we just throw mario  leona at them i am so glad she's back  and actually  inviting her to the party is by far the  best thing that knocked has done for  black clover and while there are all  sorts of other intriguing things  happening here and there it's difficult  to put any of that into perspective  at the moment because this is the limit  of what we have to work with from here  on out black clover is a weekly  experience and i'm sure that we have a  long  long way to go before this arc comes  anywhere near close to ending but i  would like to take this opportunity to  say that black clover to this point has  been a great journey i very much delayed  reading black clover because  well let's be honest it doesn't have the  greatest of impressions in the wider  anime manga fanbase i kept hearing about  how bad the anime was and just  consistent [ __ ] on the series itself  in general so naturally i put it off and  while i can't speak for the anime  because i still haven't seen  any of it such comments regarding the  manga are complete nonsense  in a way black clover is the perfect  example of a well-crafted modern shonen  series it's certainly not the greatest  that history has to offer but  also not everything needs to be in fact  when you think about it at any given  time  only one thing can actually be that so  what happens to everything else they are  rendered meaningless  definitely not my mantra whilst reading  black clover has always been to just sit  back and enjoy whatever it is that comes  my way which  i feel like has worked out pretty well  tarbata is an absolute genius with  crafting  implementing and exploring characters in  particular i can't even count the amount  of primary and secondary figures we've  been introduced to but i can say that i  do legitimately care for the large  majority of them because tarbeta has  found a way to make me do so and that is  not at all an easy thing to accomplish  and yes i do have criticisms like a lot  of criticism some of which are bigger  than others but another one would be  that the world is pretty poorly built i  really do wish we took some time to  thoroughly explore cultures and give  context to locations because for example  right now  pretty much the only thing i know about  the spade kingdom is that it's very cold  there so cold that it's snowing  currently that is its only unique  distinguishing characteristic and  the same for the others as well with the  heart kingdom all i know is that it's  more natural with the diamond kingdom  then i guess they like rocks and when it  comes to the clover kingdom our home  well it doesn't feel like anything but a  super standard cut and paste location  having said  all of that though does it even matter  well you can very easily say no  no it doesn't not everything needs to be  this encyclopedic masterpiece of world  building and the same can be said for i  guess every other criticism i've brought  up during the series because in the end  absolutely none of those things made me  want to drop black clover from the very  get-go i was on board with yelling boy's  quest to become the thing that i did not  and still do not truly understand but  there is a ton  of magic in black clover courtesy of  tarmeter's grimoire heavily heavily  underrated magic that people really  should just you know  shut up and experience because in the  end it is worth it so while the series  is unlikely to be remembered very well  if at all in manga history it will at  the very least be remembered by me for  providing just a ton of fun experiences  that's kind of it and that's all it ever  needs to be in order to keep me  satisfied so thank you all for  graciously coming on this journey with  me and i hope that each and every one of  you continue to enjoy black clover as  well what do you guys think please do  leave your thoughts in the comments  below or even join my discord server and  if you're keen for some more black  clover content then please do check out  some of my other videos or even  subscribe to the channel for very maybe  regular black clover goodness delivered  straight  into your youtube feed but for now this  has been the new world review and i'll  see you next time

